# Rank 1543 / CVE-2025-67221: orjson closed serialized objects with a
# write whose capacity guard existed only in debug builds, so a
# release-mode serialization that ended exactly at the buffer
# boundary wrote its closing brace past the allocation and crashed
# sporadically (out-of-bounds write, CWE-787/CWE-131). The object
# close in src/serialize/writer/formatter.rs did
# `debug_assert_has_capacity!(writer); unsafe { writer.put_u8(b'}');
# }` -- debug_assert compiles to nothing under --release, and the
# recursive list/dict shapes in the new test (deep nesting with
# long keys) reach the exact-capacity state where the brace write
# overflows. The fixing commit (confirmed --K --
# "Fix sporadic crash on serializing object close"): the guard
# becomes `reserve_minimum!(writer);` -- an unconditional reservation
# that grows the buffer in every build before the byte is written --
# plus test_recursion.py exercising the boundary. No pool
# correction.
#
# ATTENTION, debug-only capacity guards. The defect is a bounds
# check that evaporates in release builds -- debug_assert! is
# development tooling, not a guard, and no observation distinguishes
# an enforced reservation from a debug assertion: the memory rules
# label derefs and frees, and rust's unsafe put_u8 inside a
# debug-asserted region is indistinguishable from a checked one to
# every current rule. A binding on orjson's own macros would detect
# this crate rather than the weakness. Measured on the real code:
# scanning formatter.rs reports zero findings at both revisions. No
# ENGINE-GAPS.md entry: the piece is release-mode guard vocabulary
# (which macro families enforce in release), not a localised
# construct. No definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1543 records
# the debug-asserted close and the reserved form, both asserting
# reject VYQL-MEM-006: when release-guard vocabulary lands, the
# debug-asserted form must flip to expect.

test "rank1543: the closing brace is guarded only in debug"
  lang rust
  file src/serialize/writer/formatter.rs
  reject VYQL-MEM-006
  code
  ```
  pub(crate) trait Formatter {
      unsafe fn end_object<W>(&mut self, writer: &mut W)
      where
          W: ?Sized + WriteExt + bytes::BufMut,
      {
          debug_assert_has_capacity!(writer);
          unsafe {
              writer.put_u8(b'}');
          }
      }
  }

  macro_rules! debug_assert_has_capacity {
      ($writer:expr) => {
          #[cfg(debug_assertions)]
          assert!($writer.remaining_mut() >= 1);
      };
  }
  ```

test "rank1543: the fixed revision reserves before every close"
  lang rust
  file src/serialize/writer/formatter.rs
  reject VYQL-MEM-006
  code
  ```
  pub(crate) trait Formatter {
      unsafe fn end_object<W>(&mut self, writer: &mut W)
      where
          W: ?Sized + WriteExt + bytes::BufMut,
      {
          reserve_minimum!(writer);
          unsafe {
              writer.put_u8(b'}');
          }
      }
  }

  macro_rules! reserve_minimum {
      ($writer:expr) => {
          if $writer.remaining_mut() < 1 {
              $writer.reserve(1);
          }
      };
  }
  ```
